sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch14-05> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-05--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-05--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch14-05: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.47" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.475"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.48"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The proposed distinction can be compared with other species criteria only where ranks, geography and genetic data coincide, which is a subset of organisms. Because rank assignments already encode the presence of intermediates, a checklist test is weakly discriminating. The result can show how present ranks behave and cannot establish that former connection is the only difference." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare named varieties and named species for the presence of living morphological or genetic intermediates, and for other candidate distinctions such as reproductive isolation and genetic-cluster gaps. The claim is confirmed if the presence or absence of living intermediates is the only consistent separator, and refuted if species and varieties also separate cleanly by isolation or genetic distance once intermediates are held constant." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Taxonomists already use living intermediates to decide variety versus species, so the contrast is partly the definition under test.", "Reproductive isolation and genetic clusters are not fields in these taxonomic databases and would have to be joined from separate studies.", "Fossil intermediates that would show species were formerly connected are unavailable for the great majority of living species pairs." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-05--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-05--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-05--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch14-05--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch14-05 by Grok 4.7: 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
